}_{3}\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $v$ equals $0.$ So, we must set ${t}_{1}=0.$ \n\nSince $v$ is nonzero, we can pick any ${t}_{3}\\ne 0.$ For example, setting ${t}_{3}=1$, we get\n\n$$\nv=⟨0,\\,3,\\,1⟩.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\frac{b}{c}=3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420154 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420155 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420154 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6262b847-bfad-5541-b7d9-0c48d99eb024" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420154 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186393043 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420155 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420156 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420155 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6f1edd60-137c-5af0-bf08-f3f3e9df0344" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420155 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262846 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420156 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420158 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420156 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7c175861-cf16-5bce-9a3d-7dd7700bfeb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420156 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186420153 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420157 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186420154 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420157 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8d1b2442-6684-5f23-a6d5-881beb105644" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420157 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186120224 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420158 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f1fe54dc-0b25-528c-81fb-caa7a89e418f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186420158 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186262859 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423170 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186423178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423170 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186423179 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423170 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186423180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423170 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186423181 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423170 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186423182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186423170 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921